            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Souter asked whether the decision to impose consecutive sentences requires the finding of any fact about the crimes, the circumstances, or the defendant\u2019s character."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Souter",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f2841bde5fe76e139787612a7269a63e05369e469d92506564643bb02e617743",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f2841bde5fe7-0000-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 5,
              "start": 5
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Souter, the only fact needed might be that without a consecutive sentence there would be a \u201cfree crime,\u201d questioning whether that fact falls within any of the traditional categories."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f2841bde5fe76e139787612a7269a63e05369e469d92506564643bb02e617743",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f2841bde5fe7-0000-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 8,
              "start": 8
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Stevens asked whether the petitioner\u2019s argument applied to this case."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f2841bde5fe76e139787612a7269a63e05369e469d92506564643bb02e617743",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f2841bde5fe7-0000-0008"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 12,
              "start": 12
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Ginsburg, Justice Ginsburg raised a procedural impediment concerning a prior petition and the need for appellate permission."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice BREYER",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f2841bde5fe76e139787612a7269a63e05369e469d92506564643bb02e617743",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f2841bde5fe7-0001-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 30,
              "start": 30
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Breyer asked whether any precedent reads the rule in the way the parties suggest."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Souter",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f2841bde5fe76e139787612a7269a63e05369e469d92506564643bb02e617743",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f2841bde5fe7-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 41,
              "start": 41
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Souter, Justice Souter questioned whether the State\u2019s position required a factual distinction not spoken of in Apprendi."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Souter",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f2841bde5fe76e139787612a7269a63e05369e469d92506564643bb02e617743",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f2841bde5fe7-0002-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 42,
              "start": 42
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Souter followed with a question asking whether drawing such a distinction was required."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Souter",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f2841bde5fe76e139787612a7269a63e05369e469d92506564643bb02e617743",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f2841bde5fe7-0002-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 47,
              "start": 47
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Souter asked whether the State\u2019s claim was true in fact."
      }
