  "overview": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioner",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f2841bde5fe76e139787612a7269a63e05369e469d92506564643bb02e617743",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f2841bde5fe7-0000-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 6,
              "start": 6
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioner, petitioner cites a Washington Court of Appeals decision (State v. Washington, 143 P.3d 606) that held consecutive sentences trigger and violate Blakely."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioner",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f2841bde5fe76e139787612a7269a63e05369e469d92506564643bb02e617743",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f2841bde5fe7-0000-0007"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 11,
              "start": 11
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Petitioner argues that any additional fact needed to impose consecutive sentences must be proved to a jury beyond a reasonable doubt, following Apprendi\u2011Blakely precedent."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "State",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f2841bde5fe76e139787612a7269a63e05369e469d92506564643bb02e617743",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f2841bde5fe7-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 20,
              "start": 20
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The State (respondent) argues that precedent is clear: the statutory maximum for Sixth and Fourteenth Amendment purposes is the maximum a defendant may receive based solely on the facts reflected in the jury verdict."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f2841bde5fe76e139787612a7269a63e05369e469d92506564643bb02e617743",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f2841bde5fe7-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 21,
              "start": 21
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Court notes that none of the authorities cited by the parties quote or acknowledge the passages in Apprendi that define the test as one of effect, not form."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f2841bde5fe76e139787612a7269a63e05369e469d92506564643bb02e617743",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f2841bde5fe7-0001-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 22,
              "start": 22
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Court further observes that the holding of Apprendi is central to the issue at hand."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Overview",
    "status": "complete",
    "summary": null,
    "summary_citations": []
