                "end": 43,
                "start": 43
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to United States (amicus curiae), according to United States (amicus curiae), the United States amicus argues that a distinction could be drawn between Apprendi and Blakely, and that reasonable jurists might accept that distinction."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "United States (amicus curiae)",
